# MOVED 2026-08-16 — Michael. The union-merge rules that lived here from 2026-07-31 are gone, and
# nothing replaced them in this repository, because there is nothing here for them to apply to.
#
# They named `.claude/work/decisions.md`, `.claude/work/collab.md` and
# `.claude/work/collab_settled.md`. On 2026-08-16 `.claude/` became its own repository
# (`md12ol/GET-claude`, GitHub #74) and this repository's `.gitignore` stopped tracking it. Git
# reads `.gitattributes` only from the repository that CONTAINS the file being merged, so from that
# moment these three lines could never fire again: the merges happen inside GET-claude, which had
# no `.gitattributes` at all.
#
# The effect was silent and lasted until it was measured — two `decisions.md` entries appended from
# separate machines produced a real conflict, on files documented as never conflicting. The rules
# now live at GET-claude's own root with the prefix stripped (`work/decisions.md merge=union`),
# carrying the full reasoning: which three files keep union, why `traps.md`, `hotfixes.md` and
# `issues.md` were narrowed out of it on 2026-08-04, and why `deferred.md` was never added.
#
# Do not restore them here. A path this repository does not track cannot be given an attribute.

# Shell scripts are checked out with LF regardless of core.autocrlf. Added 2026-08-13 — Michael,
# after `sudo ./serve.sh` in WSL failed with `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`.
# Both owners' Windows clones have core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every .sh to CRLF on
# checkout; the shebang then names an interpreter called `bash\r`, which does not exist. Without
# this line the fix is not durable: the next checkout, merge or stash puts the CRs straight back.
#
# This still applies here — `documentation/serve.sh` is the case that found it. The hooks that used
# to be covered by it moved to GET-claude, which now carries its own copy of this rule.
*.sh text eol=lf
